We use vocabulary from "The Part-Time Parliament" by Leslie Lamport.

Address must contain no space or underscore.
Id must contain no space.
Decree and result must be message.mangled.

Usage:
	Ping priestId=<id> dn=<decree-number> result=<address,...>
	Propose decree=<decree>
	NextBallot dn=<decree-number> bn=<ballot-number>
	LastVote priestId=<id> dn=<decree-number> bn=<ballot-number> decree=<decree>
	Nak dn=<decree-number> bn=<ballot-number>
	DecreeNumberTooOld dn=<decree-number>
	BeginBallot dn=<decree-number> bn=<ballot-number> decree=<decree>
	Voted priestId=<id> dn=<decree-number> bn=<ballot-number> decree=<decree>
	Success dn=<decree-number> decree=<decree>
	Result dn=<decree-number> decree=<decree> result=<result>
	Redirect result=<address>
	GetLeader
	GetState
	State dn=<decree-number> result=<url>
	SubtractPriest priestId=<id> result=<id>
	WantToJoin priestId=<id>
	WantToJoinReply result=<0 or 1>

NextBallot/Nak/LastVote with negative dn means all decree-numbers >= -dn.

Client to Priest:
	Propose
	GetLeader

Priest to Client:
	Result
	Redirect

Priest to Priest:
	All of them

Decree:
	"Null" is the null decree.
	predicate* Put filename offset value
	predicate* Get filename offset size
	predicate* Stat filename
	predicate* Remove filename
	predicate* GetPriestSet
	The empty string is the olive day decree.
	Predicate:
		If filename decree-number
		Tag tag
